<BaseLayout title="Technology | Blutech Building IoT & AIoT" description="How Blutech combines privacy-preserving sensing, wireless connectivity, edge automation, Halo, Core and open integration for real buildings." canonicalPath="/technology">
  <section class="page-hero"><div class="shell"><div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span>›</span><span>Technology</span></div><div class="kicker">Architecture</div><h1>No single sensor. No single protocol. One practical system.</h1><p>Building technology works when sensing, connectivity, response time, privacy, installation constraints and integration boundaries are designed together.</p></div></section>
  <section><div class="shell"><div class="grid grid-3"><div class="card"><div class="meta">Sense</div><h3>Privacy-preserving perception</h3><p>Thermal arrays, PIR, mmWave and sensor fusion are used where conventional identifiable video is unsuitable or unnecessary.</p></div><div class="card"><div class="meta">Connect</div><h3>Protocol by purpose</h3><p>LoRaWAN for long-range low-power data, Bluetooth for immediate local interaction, plus 4G, Wi-Fi, Ethernet, RS485 and contact interfaces.</p></div><div class="card"><div class="meta">Act</div><h3>Edge automation</h3><p>Local sensor-to-controller logic can handle time-sensitive actions without depending on a round trip to the cloud.</p></div><div class="card"><div class="meta">Manage</div><h3>Blutech Core</h3><p>Provision devices, map locations, monitor connectivity, manage configuration and expose integration-ready data.</p></div><div class="card"><div class="meta">Operate</div><h3>Blutech Halo</h3><p>Give FM and operations teams live status, alerts, floorplans, history, reports and authorised controls.</p></div><div class="card"><div class="meta">Integrate</div><h3>APIs & building systems</h3><p>REST, MQTT and project-specific interfaces connect Blutech with BMS, FM, hospital and customer systems where approved.</p></div></div></div></section>
  <section style="background:var(--bg-2)"><div class="shell split"><div><div class="kicker">AI where it earns its place</div><h2>AI is a tool, not the company description.</h2><p class="hero-copy" style="font-size:19px">Blutech uses AI selectively where it adds measurable technical value — for example sensor fusion, recognition or optimisation workflows. Many reliable building functions are better served by deterministic sensing, thresholds and edge logic.</p></div><div class="panel"><h3>Design principle</h3><p class="muted">Choose the simplest architecture that meets the operational requirement, then add intelligence only where it improves accuracy, response or efficiency.</p></div></div></section>
  <section><div class="shell"><div class="section-head"><div><div class="kicker">Typical data flow</div><h2>Field → Core → Halo → building team.</h2></div></div><div class="grid grid-4"><div class="card"><h3>1. Field device</h3><p>Sensor, contact, meter, controller or third-party equipment produces a state or measurement.</p></div><div class="card"><h3>2. Connectivity</h3><p>Data travels by the network best suited to range, power, latency and site conditions.</p></div><div class="card"><h3>3. Blutech Core</h3><p>Device identity, data mapping, health, settings, rules and interfaces are managed centrally.</p></div><div class="card"><h3>4. Blutech Halo</h3><p>Operators see context and act through dashboards, alerts, reports or integrated building systems.</p></div></div></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
